# Line endings for the docs subtree.
#
# The repository root uses `* text=auto`, which stores LF but checks out CRLF on
# Windows. That makes markdown show whole-file diffs whenever a contributor on
# another platform touches it. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree LF
# everywhere, which also matches what MkDocs and CI expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Docs media in Git LFS.
#
# Scoped to this directory so it travels with the Docs subtree when it is
# pushed to the published docs repo, and does not change how the rest of the
# project stores binaries. Rules here override the repository-root
# .gitattributes for paths under Docs/.
#
# These lines must stay AFTER the `*` rule above: the last matching line wins
# per attribute, so `-text` here is what exempts binaries from LF conversion.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
